<title>USA: Pentagon - mergers like Boeing's make sense.</title>
<headline>Pentagon - mergers like Boeing's make sense.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense Department said Tuesday that mergers like the one proposed between Boeing and McDonnell Douglas make sense so long as competition continues.</p>
<p>&quot;The department recognizes that consolidation of the defense industry is both inevitable and necessary as the defense budget has declined,&quot; a spokesman, Capt. Mike Doubleday, said.&quot;Consolidating and restructuring make good sense, as long as we continue to have competition.&quot;</p>
<p>He said at a Pentagon briefing he did not know how long it would take a defense team to determine whether the Boeing and McDonnell Douglas merger would hurt competition.</p>
</text>
